  "mechanisms": [
    "Place satisfaction mediates the relationship between accessibility (perceived and spatial) and place attachment, suggesting that accessibility enhances attachment only when users are satisfied with the place.",
    "Perceived accessibility is more influential than spatial accessibility in explaining place attachment because it incorporates subjective experiences, emotions, and individual needs, which are crucial for forming emotional connections to places.",
    "Travel cost is a significant component of perceived accessibility, as high costs (time, money, effort) reduce willingness to travel and thus perceived ease of access.",
    "Longer residency fosters greater familiarity with the environment, leading to higher perceived accessibility, satisfaction, and attachment due to adaptation, integration, and emotional ties.",
    "Age and education level influence place satisfaction due to differing needs, knowledge bases, and expectations regarding urban spaces."
  ],
  "moderators": [
    "Age",
    "Education Level",
    "Length of Residence"
  ],
  "implementation_implications": [
    "Reduce travel costs and improve transportation accessibility to urban public open spaces (POS) through public transport investment, subsidies for low-income groups, and incentives for environmentally friendly modes (cycling, walking).",
    "Integrate residential areas and POS through scientific urban planning to reduce travel distances and enhance convenience.",
    "Enhance residents' emotional attachment by improving POS accessibility and addressing the mismatch between perceived and actual accessibility through better communication and design.",
    "Improve place satisfaction by focusing on pleasure, safety, comfort, and convenience in POS design, including skillful landscape design, effective lighting, surveillance, and multifunctional plans.",
    "Prioritize perceived accessibility in urban planning and policy-making by actively engaging with community residents to understand their needs and leveraging big data (social media, mobile app data) to capture real-time user feedback and behavioral patterns.",
    "Establish regular assessment mechanisms for urban planning and policies, adjusting them based on resident feedback and actual circumstances to ensure alignment with community needs."
  ],
